  "id": "labeled-lines",
  "term": "labeled lines",
  "definition": "Labeled lines are a neural coding pattern in which a neuron’s strongest response marks a particular stimulus feature. In the cortex, this can appear as signed labeled lines, where two different neurons represent opposite directions or values of the same quantitative feature.",
